<AddOnInstructionDefinition Name="SCLP" Revision="1.0" Vendor="Rockwell Automation" ExecutePrescan="false" ExecutePostscan="false" ExecuteEnableInFalse="false" CreatedDate="2007-01-11T20:25:15.926Z" CreatedBy="NA\Rockwell" EditedDate="2007-01-17T19:10:36.176Z" EditedBy="NA\Rockwell" SoftwareRevision="v16.00"
>
<Description>
<![CDATA[Scale with Parameters (given rate and offset)]]>
</Description>
<AdditionalHelpText>
<![CDATA[This routine performs the operation of the SLC-500 Scale With Parameters instruction (SCL).

Use this instruction to scale data from your analog module and bring it into the limits prescribed by the process variable or another analog module.  For example, use SCL to convert a 4-20 mA input signal to a PID process variable.  Or use SCL to scale an analog input to control an analog output.

When rung conditions are true, this instruction multiplies the source by a specified rate.  The rounded result is added to an offset value and placed in the destination.

Scaled value = (input value x rate) + offset
]]>
</AdditionalHelpText>
<Parameters>
<Parameter Name="EnableIn" DataType="BOOL" Usage="Input" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="false">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Enable Input - System Defined Parameter]]>
</Description>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="EnableOut" DataType="BOOL" Usage="Output" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="false">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Enable Output - System Defined Parameter]]>
</Description>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Source" DataType="REAL" Usage="Input" Radix="Float" Required="true" Visible="true">
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><DataValue DataType="REAL" Radix="Float" Value="0.0"/>
</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Rate" DataType="REAL" Usage="Input" Radix="Float" Required="true" Visible="true">
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><DataValue DataType="REAL" Radix="Float" Value="0.0"/>
</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Offset" DataType="REAL" Usage="Input" Radix="Float" Required="true" Visible="true">
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><DataValue DataType="REAL" Radix="Float" Value="0.0"/>
</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Destination" DataType="REAL" Usage="Output" Radix="Float" Required="true" Visible="true">
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><DataValue DataType="REAL" Radix="Float" Value="0.0"/>
</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
</Parameters>
<LocalTags>
<LocalTag Name="Temp1" DataType="REAL" Radix="Float">
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><DataValue DataType="REAL" Radix="Float" Value="0.0"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
</LocalTags>
<Routines>
<Routine Name="Logic" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[
This routine performs the operation of the SLC-500 Scale With Parameters instruction (SCL).

Use this instruction to scale data from your analog module and bring it into the limits prescribed by the process variable or another analog module.  For example, use SCL to convert a 4-20 mA input signal to a PID process variable.  Or use SCL to scale an analog input to control an analog output.

When rung conditions are true, this instruction multiplies the source by a specified rate.  The rounded result is added to an offset value and placed in the destination.

Scaled value = (input value x rate) + offset
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Scaled value = (input value x rate) + offset]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MUL(Source,Rate,Temp1)ADD(Temp1,Offset,Destination);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
</Routines>
</AddOnInstructionDefinition>
<AddOnInstructionDefinition Name="SCP" Revision="1.0" Vendor="Rockwell Automation" ExecutePrescan="false" ExecutePostscan="false" ExecuteEnableInFalse="false" CreatedDate="2007-01-11T20:06:39.002Z" CreatedBy="NA\Rockwell" EditedDate="2007-01-17T19:10:56.520Z" EditedBy="NA\Rockwell" SoftwareRevision="v16.00"
>
<Description>
<![CDATA[Scale with Parameters]]>
</Description>
<AdditionalHelpText>
<![CDATA[This instruction performs the operation of the SLC-500 Scale With Parameters instruction (SCP).

This output instruction consists of six parameters.  Parameters may be immediate data values or tags containing values.  The Input value is scaled to a range determined by creating a linear relationship between input min and max values and scaled min and max values.  The scaled result is returned to the tag indicated by the output parameter.

The formula is as follows:
Scaled value = (input value x rate) + offset
Rate = (scaled max. - scaled min.) / (input max. - input min.)
Offset = scaled minimum - (input minimum x rate)
]]>
</AdditionalHelpText>
<Parameters>
<Parameter Name="EnableIn" DataType="BOOL" Usage="Input" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="false">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Enable Input - System Defined Parameter]]>
</Description>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="EnableOut" DataType="BOOL" Usage="Output" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="false">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Enable Output - System Defined Parameter]]>
</Description>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Input" DataType="REAL" Usage="Input" Radix="Float" Required="true" Visible="true">
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><DataValue DataType="REAL" Radix="Float" Value="0.0"/>
</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="InputMin" DataType="REAL" Usage="Input" Radix="Float" Required="true" Visible="true">
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><DataValue DataType="REAL" Radix="Float" Value="0.0"/>
</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="InputMax" DataType="REAL" Usage="Input" Radix="Float" Required="true" Visible="true">
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><DataValue DataType="REAL" Radix="Float" Value="0.0"/>
</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="ScaledMin" DataType="REAL" Usage="Input" Radix="Float" Required="true" Visible="true">
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><DataValue DataType="REAL" Radix="Float" Value="0.0"/>
</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="ScaledMax" DataType="REAL" Usage="Input" Radix="Float" Required="true" Visible="true">
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><DataValue DataType="REAL" Radix="Float" Value="0.0"/>
</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Output" DataType="REAL" Usage="Output" Radix="Float" Required="true" Visible="true">
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><DataValue DataType="REAL" Radix="Float" Value="0.0"/>
</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
</Parameters>
<LocalTags>
<LocalTag Name="Temp4" DataType="REAL" Radix="Float">
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><DataValue DataType="REAL" Radix="Float" Value="0.0"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Temp3" DataType="REAL" Radix="Float">
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><DataValue DataType="REAL" Radix="Float" Value="0.0"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Temp2" DataType="REAL" Radix="Float">
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><DataValue DataType="REAL" Radix="Float" Value="0.0"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Temp1" DataType="REAL" Radix="Float">
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><DataValue DataType="REAL" Radix="Float" Value="0.0"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Offset" DataType="REAL" Radix="Float">
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><DataValue DataType="REAL" Radix="Float" Value="0.0"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Rate" DataType="REAL" Radix="Float">
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><DataValue DataType="REAL" Radix="Float" Value="0.0"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Out" DataType="REAL" Radix="Float">
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><DataValue DataType="REAL" Radix="Float" Value="0.0"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
</LocalTags>
<Routines>
<Routine Name="Logic" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[
This routine performs the operation of the SLC-500 Scale With Parameters instruction (SCP).

This output instruction consists of six parameters.  Parameters may be integer immediate data values or tags containing values.  The Input value is scaled to a range determined by creating a linear relationship between input min and max values and scaled min and max values.  The scaled result is returned to the tag indicated by the output parameter.

The formula is as follows:
Scaled value = (input value x rate) + offset
Rate = (scaled max. - scaled min.) / (input max. - input min.)
Offset = scaled minimum - (input minimum x rate)
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Rate = (scaled max. - scaled min.) / (input max. - input min.)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[SUB(ScaledMax,ScaledMin,Temp1)SUB(InputMax,InputMin,Temp2)DIV(Temp1,Temp2,Rate);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Offset = scaled minimum - (input minimum x rate)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MUL(InputMin,Rate,Temp3)SUB(ScaledMin,Temp3,Offset);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Scaled value = (input value x rate) + offset]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MUL(Input,Rate,Temp4)ADD(Temp4,Offset,Output);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
</Routines>
</AddOnInstructionDefinition>
<AddOnInstructionDefinition Name="TankLevelSimulation" Revision="1.0" Vendor="Rockwell Automation" ExecutePrescan="false" ExecutePostscan="false" ExecuteEnableInFalse="false" CreatedDate="2007-01-16T21:53:00.088Z" CreatedBy="NA\Rockwell" EditedDate="2007-01-17T19:20:55.168Z" EditedBy="NA\Rockwell" SoftwareRevision="v16.00"
>
<Description>
<![CDATA[Simulates the level in a tank based on an inlet flow rate and outlet flow rate.  Must run in a periodic task.]]>
</Description>
<AdditionalHelpText>
<![CDATA[This instruction must run in a periodic task.

To use this instruction, first add up all the input flows to the tank and feed that value into FlowIntoTank.  Add up all the outlet flows from the tank and feed that value into FlowOutOfTank.  The engineering units of FlowIntoTank and FlowOutOfTank must match.  Then select the FlowTimeBase to match the flow engineering units.  For example, if the flows are given in Gallons per Minute, you would select 1=minutes for the FlowTimeBase.

Then enter the TankCapacity in whatever units you use to measure your tank volume.  You can use the Gain parameter to convert your flow input units to the correct tank volume units.  For example, if your flows are in Gallons per Minute, and your tank is a 10,000 liter tank, you would enter 10,000 for TankCapacity and 3.785 for Gain.  Your tank level would then be correctly simulated in liters.

If you wish to reset your simulation and empty the tank, you can set the EmptyTank input.  This will force the simulated TankLevel to equal zero when EmptyTank transitions to set.  If you want to empty the tank again, you will need to transition EmptyTank from false to true.]]>
</AdditionalHelpText>
<Parameters>
<Parameter Name="EnableIn" DataType="BOOL" Usage="Input" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="false">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Enable Input - System Defined Parameter]]>
</Description>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="EnableOut" DataType="BOOL" Usage="Output" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="false">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Enable Output - System Defined Parameter]]>
</Description>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="FlowIntoTank" DataType="REAL" Usage="Input" Radix="Float" Required="false" Visible="true">
<Description>
<![CDATA[The flow into the simulated tank.  Must have the same units as FlowOutOfTank.]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><DataValue DataType="REAL" Radix="Float" Value="0.0"/>
</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="FlowOutOfTank" DataType="REAL" Usage="Input" Radix="Float" Required="false" Visible="true">
<Description>
<![CDATA[The flow out of the simulated tank.  Must have the same units as FlowIntoTank.]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><DataValue DataType="REAL" Radix="Float" Value="0.0"/>
</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="FlowTimeBase" DataType="DINT" Usage="Input" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="false">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Select the time base used for the flow inputs.  Enter 0 for seconds, 1 for minutes, 2 for hours, 3 for days.]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>01 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><DataValue DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="1"/>
</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="TankCapacity" DataType="REAL" Usage="Input" Radix="Float" Required="false" Visible="false">
<Description>
<![CDATA[The tank volume.]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><DataValue DataType="REAL" Radix="Float" Value="0.0"/>
</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Gain" DataType="REAL" Usage="Input" Radix="Float" Required="false" Visible="false">
<Description>
<![CDATA[A gain value which can be used to convert flow units into TankCapacity units.  (eg. Gallons  into Liters)]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00 00 80 3F</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><DataValue DataType="REAL" Radix="Float" Value="1.0"/>
</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="EmptyTank" DataType="BOOL" Usage="Input" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="false">
<Description>
<![CDATA[A switch to immediately empty the simulation tank.  The tank will empty when EmptyTank transitions to true.]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><DataValue DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="TankLevel" DataType="REAL" Usage="Output" Radix="Float" Required="false" Visible="true">
<Description>
<![CDATA[The level in the simulated tank.]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><DataValue DataType="REAL" Radix="Float" Value="0.0"/>
</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
</Parameters>
