<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
T_LEQ:  TIME -- LESS THAN OR EQUAL
============================================================
Revision 1.0-Example:  2008-Jul-02, DER
Release for V17 CD as Date/Time Examples
============================================================
Returns TRUE (1) in EnableOut and Out if Ref_DT1 is LESS THAN
OR EQUAL TO (before or the same as) Ref_DT2
============================================================
POWERUP / INVALID STATE HANDLING
============================================================
This logic determines a comparison result every scan when enabled
(and sets EnableOut and Out to 0 every scan if on a False Rung or if EnableIn is cleared).
No powerup or invalid state handling is necessary.
============================================================
NORMALIZE THE INPUT DATES/TIMES
============================================================
This rung adds each of the input Date/Time parameters to a .
 The T_ADD instruction  its output to:
0 <= microseconds < 1.000,000
0 <= seconds < 60
0 <= minutes < 60
0 <= hours < 24
1 <= days <= 31 (and day is valid for calendar month/year)
1 <= months <= 12
valid years are about +/- 5.8 million

Remember that if A <= B, then A+C <= B+C, so we are OK to add.  And
it works if what we're adding is a Date/Time OR an Amount of Time!!!]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[CLR(Wrk_Null.Yr) CLR(Wrk_Null.Mo) CLR(Wrk_Null.Da) ,CLR(Wrk_Null.Hr) CLR(Wrk_Null.Min) CLR(Wrk_Null.Sec) ,CLR(Wrk_Null.uSec) T_ADD(Wrk_TADD_DT1,Wrk_Null,Ref_DT1,Wrk_DT1) T_ADD(Wrk_TADD_DT2,Wrk_Null,Ref_DT2,Wrk_DT2) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
COMPARE Wrk_DT1 <= Wrk_DT2
============================================================
Now that the two input parameters have been :
IF the Wrk_DT1 YEAR is lower,
or if the years are the same and the Wrk_DT1 MONTH is lower,
or if the years and months are the same and the Wrk_DT1 DAY is lower,
or if the years, months and days are the same and the Wrk_DT1 HOUR is lower,
or if the years, months, days and hours are the same and the Wrk_DT1 MINUTE is lower,
or if the years, months, days, hours and minutes are the same and the Wrk_DT1 SECOND is lower,
or if the years, months, days, hours, minutes and seconds are the same and the Wrk_DT1 MICROSECOND is lower or the SAME,
(whew!)  THEN Wrk_DT1 is BEFORE OR THE SAME AS (less than or equal to) Wrk_DT2,
and so Ref_DT1 is less than or equal to Ref_DT2.

(NOTE: You can type <ALT>- 0 (zero) or click the  icon on the toolbar
to close the Controller Organizer tree if you would like a wider view of this rung.)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[LES(Wrk_DT1.Yr,Wrk_DT2.Yr) ,EQU(Wrk_DT1.Yr,Wrk_DT2.Yr) [LES(Wrk_DT1.Mo,Wrk_DT2.Mo) ,EQU(Wrk_DT1.Mo,Wrk_DT2.Mo) [LES(Wrk_DT1.Da,Wrk_DT2.Da) ,EQU(Wrk_DT1.Da,Wrk_DT2.Da) [LES(Wrk_DT1.Hr,Wrk_DT2.Hr) ,EQU(Wrk_DT1.Hr,Wrk_DT2.Hr) [LES(Wrk_DT1.Min,Wrk_DT2.Min) ,EQU(Wrk_DT1.Min,Wrk_DT2.Min) [LES(Wrk_DT1.Sec,Wrk_DT2.Sec) ,EQU(Wrk_DT1.Sec,Wrk_DT2.Sec) LEQ(Wrk_DT1.uSec,Wrk_DT2.uSec) ] ] ] ] ] ]OTE(EnableOut)OTE(Wrk_Out);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Normally there would be an OTE of  on the rung above,
but because we unlatch (OTU) the Out bit in the EnableInFalse routine,
we need to have all  references be OTL or OTU in order to avoid
an annoying verification Warning (duplicate destructive bit reference).
This warning appears in the user program even if this AOI is locked down....]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Wrk_Out) OTL(Out) ,XIO(Wrk_Out) OTU(Out) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
</Routines>
</AddOnInstructionDefinition>
<AddOnInstructionDefinition Name="T_LIM" Revision="1.0" RevisionExtension="Example" Vendor="Rockwell Automation" ExecutePrescan="false" ExecutePostscan="false" ExecuteEnableInFalse="true" CreatedDate="2008-04-15T14:24:48.205Z" CreatedBy="NA\dereed" EditedDate="2008-07-02T16:35:41.488Z" EditedBy="NA\dereed"
 SoftwareRevision="v16.03">
<Description>
<![CDATA[DateTime Limit Test]]>
</Description>
<RevisionNote>
<![CDATA[Release for V17 CD as Date/Time Examples]]>
</RevisionNote>
<AdditionalHelpText>
<![CDATA[This instruction compares a Date-and-Time-of-Day or amount of time with
a High Limit (Date/Time or amount of time) and a Low Limit (Date/Time or amount of time)

There are two cases: a  (Low Limt <= High Limt) and a  (Low Limit > High Limit)
In the normal case, EnableOut and Out are set if:
    Low Limit  <= DateTime <= High Limit
In the circular case, EnableOut and Out are set if:
    DateTime >= Low Limit   OR  DateTime <= HighLimit  (remember, High Limit < Low Limit !)

This instruction may be used in Ladder Diagram, Structured Text
or Function Block Routines just like the LIM instruction
is used for integers and floating point numbers.  However,
because it has InOut Parameters (tag references to user-defined
types), it is NOT left-justified on ladder rungs!

On a False rung in LD, or in FBD with EnableIn cleared to 0, Out is cleared to 0.

***** NOTE: THIS INSTRUCTION IS DEPENDENT ON THE
USER-DEFINED TYPE  (EXTERNAL TO THIS ADD-ON
INSTRUCTION DEFINITION)!  

 IS DEFINED AS:

  Yr : DINT  (year)
  Mo : DINT  (month)
  Da : DINT  (day)
  Hr : DINT  (hour)
  Min : DINT  (minute)
  Sec : DINT  (second)
  uSec : DINT  (microsecond)]]>
</AdditionalHelpText>
<Parameters>
<Parameter Name="EnableIn" DataType="BOOL" Usage="Input" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="false">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Enable Input - System Defined Parameter]]>
</Description>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="EnableOut" DataType="BOOL" Usage="Output" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="false">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Enable Output - System Defined Parameter]]>
</Description>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Ref_DT_LoLim" DataType="DateTime" Usage="InOut" Required="true" Visible="true">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Date and TimeOfDay Low Limit Value]]>
</Description>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Ref_DT" DataType="DateTime" Usage="InOut" Required="true" Visible="true">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Date and TimeOfDay input for compare]]>
</Description>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Ref_DT_HiLim" DataType="DateTime" Usage="InOut" Required="true" Visible="true">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Date and TimeOfDay High Limit Value]]>
</Description>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Out" DataType="BOOL" Usage="Output" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="true">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Result 1 if DT is within limits (circular)]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><DataValue DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
</Parameters>
<LocalTags>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_TLEQ" DataType="T_LEQ">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Backing Tag for T_LEQ instruction]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>01 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 01 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
01 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><Structure DataType="T_LEQ">
<DataValueMember Name="EnableIn" DataType="BOOL" Value="1"/>
<DataValueMember Name="EnableOut" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Out" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
</Structure>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_TLES" DataType="T_LES">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Backing Tag for T_LES instruction]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>01 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 01 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
01 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><Structure DataType="T_LES">
<DataValueMember Name="EnableIn" DataType="BOOL" Value="1"/>
<DataValueMember Name="EnableOut" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Out" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
</Structure>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_TGEQ" DataType="T_GEQ">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Backing Tag for T_GEQ instruction]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>01 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 01 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
01 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><Structure DataType="T_GEQ">
<DataValueMember Name="EnableIn" DataType="BOOL" Value="1"/>
<DataValueMember Name="EnableOut" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Out" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
</Structure>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_Out" DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Work Register: internal Output]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><DataValue DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_HiLim_LT_LoLim" DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Records that the High Limit is less than the Low Limit]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><DataValue DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_DT_LE_HiLim" DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Records that DT is less than or equal to the High Limit]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><DataValue DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_DT_GE_LoLim" DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Records that DT is greater than or equal to the Low Limit]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><DataValue DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
</LocalTags>
<Routines>
<Routine Name="EnableInFalse" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[If rung is false, clear output ]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
ENABLE-IN FALSE LOGIC
============================================================
When EnableIn is false (false rung in LD, input of 0 in FBD),
the main Logic Routine is not scanned, and the output  is
not cleared.  We need this Routine to Clear  in that case.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTU(Out);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="Logic" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Compare: LoLim <= DT <= HiLim]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
T_LIM:  TIME -- LIMIT CHECK
============================================================
Revision 1.0-Example:  2008-Jul-02, DER
Release for V17 CD as Date/Time Examples
============================================================
Returns TRUE (1) in EnableOut and Out if:

when DT_HiLim >= DT_LoLim:      DT_LoLim <= Ref_DT <= DT_HiLim
when DT_HiLim < DT_LoLim:      Ref_DT >= DT_LoLim   OR   Ref_DT <= DT_HiLim
(circular comparison -- see LIM instruction documentation for details!!!)
============================================================
POWERUP / INVALID STATE HANDLING
============================================================
This logic determines a comparison result every scan when enabled
(and sets EnableOut and Out to 0 every scan if on a False Rung or if EnableIn is cleared).
No powerup or invalid state handling is necessary.
============================================================
DO THE DATE/TIME COMPARES AND RECORD RESULTS
============================================================
This rung performs all the Date/Time comparisons needed and records the
results for use in the next rung.  Needed results are:

1.  Is DT_HiLim less than (before) DT_LoLim?
2.  Is the reference DT less than or equal to DT_HiLim?
3.  Is the reference DT greater than or equal to DT_LoLim?]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[T_LES(Wrk_TLES,Ref_DT_HiLim,Ref_DT_LoLim) OTE(Wrk_HiLim_LT_LoLim) ,T_LEQ(Wrk_TLEQ,Ref_DT,Ref_DT_HiLim) OTE(Wrk_DT_LE_HiLim) ,T_GEQ(Wrk_TGEQ,Ref_DT,Ref_DT_LoLim) OTE(Wrk_DT_GE_LoLim) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
BASED ON RESULTS, DETERMINE OUTPUT
============================================================
The upper input branch is the normal comparison case, where DT_LoLim  <= DT_HiLim:
True if    ( DT_LoLim  <=  Ref_DT )  AND  ( Ref_DT  <=  DT_HiLim )

The lower input branch is the  (reversed limits) case, where DT_LoLim > DT_HiLim:
True if    ( DT_LoLim  <=  Ref_DT )   OR   (Ref_DT  <=  DT_HiLim )]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Wrk_HiLim_LT_LoLim) XIC(Wrk_DT_LE_HiLim) XIC(Wrk_DT_GE_LoLim) ,XIC(Wrk_HiLim_LT_LoLim) [XIC(Wrk_DT_LE_HiLim) ,XIC(Wrk_DT_GE_LoLim) ] ]OTE(EnableOut)OTE(Wrk_Out);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Normally there would be an OTE of  on the rung above,
but because we unlatch (OTU) the Out bit in the EnableInFalse routine,
we need to have all  references be OTL or OTU in order to avoid
an annoying verification Warning (duplicate destructive bit reference).
This warning appears in the user program even if this AOI is locked down....]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Wrk_Out) OTL(Out) ,XIO(Wrk_Out) OTU(Out) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
</Routines>
</AddOnInstructionDefinition>
<AddOnInstructionDefinition Name="T_GRT" Revision="1.0" RevisionExtension="Example" Vendor="Rockwell Automation" ExecutePrescan="false" ExecutePostscan="false" ExecuteEnableInFalse="true" CreatedDate="2006-07-27T19:19:22.981Z" CreatedBy="NA\dereed" EditedDate="2008-07-02T16:34:25.939Z" EditedBy="NA\dereed"
 SoftwareRevision="v16.03">
<Description>
<![CDATA[DateTime > DateTime?]]>
</Description>
<RevisionNote>
<![CDATA[Release for V17 CD as Date/Time Examples]]>
</RevisionNote>
<AdditionalHelpText>
<![CDATA[This instruction compares two Date-and-Time-of-Day (DateTime)
variables.

If DT1 is greater than (after) DT2, EnableOut and Out are set to true (1).
Otherwise EnableOut and Out are cleared to false (0).

This instruction may be used in Ladder Diagram, Structured Text
or Function Block Routines just like the GRT instruction
is used for integers and floating point numbers.  However,
because it has InOut Parameters (tag references to user-defined
types), it is NOT left-justified on ladder rungs!

On a False rung in LD, or in FBD with EnableIn cleared to 0, Out is cleared to 0.

***** NOTE: THIS INSTRUCTION IS DEPENDENT ON THE
USER-DEFINED TYPE  (EXTERNAL TO THIS ADD-ON
INSTRUCTION DEFINITION)!  

 IS DEFINED AS:

  Yr : DINT  (year)
  Mo : DINT  (month)
  Da : DINT  (day)
  Hr : DINT  (hour)
  Min : DINT  (minute)
  Sec : DINT  (second)
  uSec : DINT  (microsecond)]]>
</AdditionalHelpText>
<Parameters>
<Parameter Name="EnableIn" DataType="BOOL" Usage="Input" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="false">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Enable Input - System Defined Parameter]]>
</Description>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="EnableOut" DataType="BOOL" Usage="Output" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="false">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Enable Output - System Defined Parameter]]>
</Description>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Ref_DT1" DataType="DateTime" Usage="InOut" Required="true" Visible="true">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Date and Time input #1]]>
</Description>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Ref_DT2" DataType="DateTime" Usage="InOut" Required="true" Visible="true">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Date and Time input #2]]>
</Description>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Out" DataType="BOOL" Usage="Output" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="true">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Result: 1 if DT1 is Greater Than DT2]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><DataValue DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
</Parameters>
<LocalTags>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_Out" DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Work Register: internal Output]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><DataValue DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_Null" DataType="DateTime">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Null Date and Time (amount of time = 0)]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><Structure DataType="DateTime">
<DataValueMember Name="Yr" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Mo" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Da" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Hr" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Min" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Sec" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="uSec" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</Structure>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_DT2" DataType="DateTime">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Result of Ref_DT2 + T_Now]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><Structure DataType="DateTime">
<DataValueMember Name="Yr" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Mo" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Da" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Hr" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Min" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Sec" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="uSec" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</Structure>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_DT1" DataType="DateTime">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Result of Ref_DT1 + T_Now]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><Structure DataType="DateTime">
<DataValueMember Name="Yr" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Mo" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Da" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Hr" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Min" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Sec" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="uSec" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</Structure>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_TADD_DT2" DataType="T_ADD">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Backing tag for T_ADD for DT2]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>01 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><Structure DataType="T_ADD">
<DataValueMember Name="EnableIn" DataType="BOOL" Value="1"/>
<DataValueMember Name="EnableOut" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
</Structure>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_TADD_DT1" DataType="T_ADD">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Backing tag for T_ADD for DT1]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>01 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><Structure DataType="T_ADD">
<DataValueMember Name="EnableIn" DataType="BOOL" Value="1"/>
<DataValueMember Name="EnableOut" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
</Structure>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
</LocalTags>
<Routines>
<Routine Name="EnableInFalse" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[If rung is false, clear output ]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
ENABLE-IN FALSE LOGIC
============================================================
When EnableIn is false (false rung in LD, input of 0 in FBD),
the main Logic Routine is not scanned, and the output  is
not cleared.  We need this Routine to Clear  in that case.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTU(Out);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="Logic" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Compare: DT1 > DT2 ?]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
T_GRT:  TIME -- GREATER THAN
============================================================
Revision 1.0-Example:  2008-Jul-02, DER
Release for V17 CD as Date/Time Examples
============================================================
Returns TRUE (1) in EnableOut and Out if Ref_DT1 is
GREATER THAN (after) Ref_DT2
============================================================
POWERUP / INVALID STATE HANDLING
============================================================
This logic determines a comparison result every scan when enabled
(and sets EnableOut and Out to 0 every scan if on a False Rung or if EnableIn is cleared).
No powerup or invalid state handling is necessary.
============================================================
NORMALIZE THE INPUT DATES/TIMES
============================================================
This rung adds each of the input Date/Time parameters to a .
 The T_ADD instruction  its output to:
0 <= microseconds < 1.000,000
0 <= seconds < 60
0 <= minutes < 60
0 <= hours < 24
1 <= days <= 31 (and day is valid for calendar month/year)
1 <= months <= 12
valid years are about +/- 5.8 million

Remember that if A > B, then A+C > B+C, so we are OK to add.  And
it works if what we're adding is a Date/Time OR an Amount of Time!!!]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[CLR(Wrk_Null.Yr) CLR(Wrk_Null.Mo) CLR(Wrk_Null.Da) ,CLR(Wrk_Null.Hr) CLR(Wrk_Null.Min) CLR(Wrk_Null.Sec) ,CLR(Wrk_Null.uSec) T_ADD(Wrk_TADD_DT1,Wrk_Null,Ref_DT1,Wrk_DT1) T_ADD(Wrk_TADD_DT2,Wrk_Null,Ref_DT2,Wrk_DT2) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
COMPARE Wrk_DT1 > Wrk_DT2
============================================================
Now that the two input parameters have been :
IF the Wrk_DT1 YEAR is higher,
or if the years are the same and the Wrk_DT1 MONTH is higher,
or if the years and months are the same and the Wrk_DT1 DAY is higher,
or if the years, months and days are the same and the Wrk_DT1 HOUR is higher,
or if the years, months, days and hours are the same and the Wrk_DT1 MINUTE is higher,
or if the years, months, days, hours and minutes are the same and the Wrk_DT1 SECOND is higher,
or if the years, months, days, hours, minutes and seconds are the same and the Wrk_DT1 MICROSECOND is higher,
(whew!)  THEN Wrk_DT1 is AFTER (greater than) Wrk_DT2,
and so Ref_DT1 is greater than Ref_DT2.

(NOTE: You can type <ALT>- 0 (zero) or click the  icon on the toolbar
to close the Controller Organizer tree if you would like a wider view of this rung.)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[GRT(Wrk_DT1.Yr,Wrk_DT2.Yr) ,EQU(Wrk_DT1.Yr,Wrk_DT2.Yr) [GRT(Wrk_DT1.Mo,Wrk_DT2.Mo) ,EQU(Wrk_DT1.Mo,Wrk_DT2.Mo) [GRT(Wrk_DT1.Da,Wrk_DT2.Da) ,EQU(Wrk_DT1.Da,Wrk_DT2.Da) [GRT(Wrk_DT1.Hr,Wrk_DT2.Hr) ,EQU(Wrk_DT1.Hr,Wrk_DT2.Hr) [GRT(Wrk_DT1.Min,Wrk_DT2.Min) ,EQU(Wrk_DT1.Min,Wrk_DT2.Min) [GRT(Wrk_DT1.Sec,Wrk_DT2.Sec) ,EQU(Wrk_DT1.Sec,Wrk_DT2.Sec) GRT(Wrk_DT1.uSec,Wrk_DT2.uSec) ] ] ] ] ] ]OTE(EnableOut)OTE(Wrk_Out);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Normally there would be an OTE of  on the rung above,
but because we unlatch (OTU) the Out bit in the EnableInFalse routine,
we need to have all  references be OTL or OTU in order to avoid
an annoying verification Warning (duplicate destructive bit reference).
This warning appears in the user program even if this AOI is locked down....]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Wrk_Out) OTL(Out) ,XIO(Wrk_Out) OTU(Out) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
</Routines>
</AddOnInstructionDefinition>
<AddOnInstructionDefinition Name="T_EQU" Revision="1.0" RevisionExtension="Example" Vendor="Rockwell Automation" ExecutePrescan="false" ExecutePostscan="false" ExecuteEnableInFalse="true" CreatedDate="2006-07-27T19:19:22.981Z" CreatedBy="NA\dereed" EditedDate="2008-07-02T16:33:31.843Z" EditedBy="NA\dereed"
 SoftwareRevision="v16.03">
<Description>
<![CDATA[DateTime = DateTime?]]>
</Description>
<RevisionNote>
<![CDATA[Release for V17 CD as Date/Time Examples]]>
</RevisionNote>
<AdditionalHelpText>
<![CDATA[This instruction compares two Date-and-Time-of-Day (DateTime)
variables.

If DT1 is equal to DT2, EnableOut and Out are set to true (1).
Otherwise EnableOut and Out are cleared to false (0).

This instruction may be used in Ladder Diagram, Structured Text
or Function Block Routines just like the EQU instruction
is used for integers and floating point numbers.  However,
because it has InOut Parameters (tag references to user-defined
types), it is NOT left-justified on ladder rungs!

On a False rung in LD, or in FBD with EnableIn cleared to 0, Out is cleared to 0.

***** NOTE: THIS INSTRUCTION IS DEPENDENT ON THE
USER-DEFINED TYPE  (EXTERNAL TO THIS ADD-ON
INSTRUCTION DEFINITION)!  

 IS DEFINED AS:

  Yr : DINT  (year)
  Mo : DINT  (month)
  Da : DINT  (day)
  Hr : DINT  (hour)
  Min : DINT  (minute)
  Sec : DINT  (second)
  uSec : DINT  (microsecond)]]>
</AdditionalHelpText>
<Parameters>
<Parameter Name="EnableIn" DataType="BOOL" Usage="Input" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="false">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Enable Input - System Defined Parameter]]>
</Description>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="EnableOut" DataType="BOOL" Usage="Output" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="false">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Enable Output - System Defined Parameter]]>
</Description>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Ref_DT1" DataType="DateTime" Usage="InOut" Required="true" Visible="true">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Date and Time input #1]]>
</Description>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Ref_DT2" DataType="DateTime" Usage="InOut" Required="true" Visible="true">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Date and Time input #2]]>
</Description>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Out" DataType="BOOL" Usage="Output" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="true">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Result: 1 if DT1 is Equal to DT2]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><DataValue DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
</Parameters>
<LocalTags>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_Out" DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Work Register: internal Output]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><DataValue DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_Null" DataType="DateTime">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Null Date and Time (amount of time = 0)]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><Structure DataType="DateTime">
<DataValueMember Name="Yr" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Mo" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Da" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Hr" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Min" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Sec" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="uSec" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</Structure>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_DT2" DataType="DateTime">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Result of Ref_DT2 + T_Now]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><Structure DataType="DateTime">
<DataValueMember Name="Yr" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Mo" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Da" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Hr" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Min" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Sec" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="uSec" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</Structure>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_DT1" DataType="DateTime">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Result of Ref_DT1 + T_Now]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><Structure DataType="DateTime">
<DataValueMember Name="Yr" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Mo" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Da" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Hr" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Min" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Sec" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="uSec" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</Structure>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_TADD_DT2" DataType="T_ADD">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Backing tag for T_ADD for DT2]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>01 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><Structure DataType="T_ADD">
<DataValueMember Name="EnableIn" DataType="BOOL" Value="1"/>
<DataValueMember Name="EnableOut" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
</Structure>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_TADD_DT1" DataType="T_ADD">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Backing tag for T_ADD for DT1]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>01 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><Structure DataType="T_ADD">
<DataValueMember Name="EnableIn" DataType="BOOL" Value="1"/>
<DataValueMember Name="EnableOut" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
</Structure>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
</LocalTags>
<Routines>
<Routine Name="EnableInFalse" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[If rung is false, clear output ]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
ENABLE-IN FALSE LOGIC
============================================================
When EnableIn is false (false rung in LD, input of 0 in FBD),
the main Logic Routine is not scanned, and the output  is
not cleared.  We need this Routine to Clear  in that case.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTU(Out);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="Logic" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Compare: DT1 = DT2 ?]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
T_EQU:  TIME -- EQUAL TO
============================================================
Revision 1.0-Example:  2008-Jul-02, DER
Release for V17 CD as Date/Time Examples
============================================================
Returns TRUE (1) in EnableOut and Out if Ref_DT1 is GREATER THAN
OR EQUAL TO (after or the same as) Ref_DT2
============================================================
POWERUP / INVALID STATE HANDLING
============================================================
This logic determines a comparison result every scan when enabled
(and sets EnableOut and Out to 0 every scan if on a False Rung or if EnableIn is cleared).
No powerup or invalid state handling is necessary.
============================================================
NORMALIZE THE INPUT DATES/TIMES
============================================================
This rung adds each of the input Date/Time parameters to a .
 The T_ADD instruction  its output to:
0 <= microseconds < 1.000,000
0 <= seconds < 60
0 <= minutes < 60
0 <= hours < 24
1 <= days <= 31 (and day is valid for calendar month/year)
1 <= months <= 12
valid years are about +/- 5.8 million

Remember that if A = B, then A+C = B+C, so we are OK to add.  And
it works if what we're adding is a Date/Time OR an Amount of Time!!!]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[CLR(Wrk_Null.Yr) CLR(Wrk_Null.Mo) CLR(Wrk_Null.Da) ,CLR(Wrk_Null.Hr) CLR(Wrk_Null.Min) CLR(Wrk_Null.Sec) ,CLR(Wrk_Null.uSec) T_ADD(Wrk_TADD_DT1,Wrk_Null,Ref_DT1,Wrk_DT1) T_ADD(Wrk_TADD_DT2,Wrk_Null,Ref_DT2,Wrk_DT2) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
COMPARE Wrk_DT1 = Wrk_DT2
============================================================
Now that the two input parameters have been :
IF the Wrk_DT1 YEAR is equl to Wrk_DT2 YEAR, and
the Wrk_DT1 MONTH is equl to Wrk_DT2 MONTH, and
the Wrk_DT1 DAY is equl to Wrk_DT2 DAY, and
the Wrk_DT1 HOUR is equl to Wrk_DT2 HOUR, and
the Wrk_DT1 MINUTE is equl to Wrk_DT2 MINUTE, and
the Wrk_DT1 SECOND is equl to Wrk_DT2 SECOND, and
the Wrk_DT1 MICROSECOND is equl to Wrk_DT2 MICROSECOND (whew!),
THEN Wrk_DT1 is THE SAME AS (equal to) Wrk_DT2,
and so Ref_DT1 is equal to Ref_DT2.

(NOTE: You can type <ALT>- 0 (zero) or click the  icon on the toolbar
to close the Controller Organizer tree if you would like a wider view of this rung.)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(Wrk_DT1.Yr,Wrk_DT2.Yr)EQU(Wrk_DT1.Mo,Wrk_DT2.Mo)EQU(Wrk_DT1.Da,Wrk_DT2.Da)EQU(Wrk_DT1.Hr,Wrk_DT2.Hr)EQU(Wrk_DT1.Min,Wrk_DT2.Min)EQU(Wrk_DT1.Sec,Wrk_DT2.Sec)EQU(Wrk_DT1.uSec,Wrk_DT2.uSec)OTE(EnableOut)OTE(Wrk_Out);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Normally there would be an OTE of  on the rung above,
but because we unlatch (OTU) the Out bit in the EnableInFalse routine,
we need to have all  references be OTL or OTU in order to avoid
an annoying verification Warning (duplicate destructive bit reference).
This warning appears in the user program even if this AOI is locked down....]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Wrk_Out) OTL(Out) ,XIO(Wrk_Out) OTU(Out) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
</Routines>
</AddOnInstructionDefinition>
<AddOnInstructionDefinition Name="T_NEQ" Revision="1.0" RevisionExtension="Example" Vendor="Rockwell Automation" ExecutePrescan="false" ExecutePostscan="false" ExecuteEnableInFalse="true" CreatedDate="2006-07-27T19:19:22.981Z" CreatedBy="NA\dereed" EditedDate="2008-07-02T16:36:06.551Z" EditedBy="NA\dereed"
 SoftwareRevision="v16.03">
<Description>
<![CDATA[DateTime <> DateTime?]]>
</Description>
<RevisionNote>
<![CDATA[Release for V17 CD as Date/Time Examples]]>
</RevisionNote>
<AdditionalHelpText>
<![CDATA[This instruction compares two Date-and-Time-of-Day (DateTime)
variables.

If DT1 is not equal to DT2, EnableOut and Out are set to true (1).
Otherwise EnableOut and Out are cleared to false (0).

This instruction may be used in Ladder Diagram, Structured Text
or Function Block Routines just like the NEQ instruction
is used for integers and floating point numbers.  However,
because it has InOut Parameters (tag references to user-defined
types), it is NOT left-justified on ladder rungs!

On a False rung in LD, or in FBD with EnableIn cleared to 0, Out is cleared to 0.

***** NOTE: THIS INSTRUCTION IS DEPENDENT ON THE
USER-DEFINED TYPE  (EXTERNAL TO THIS ADD-ON
INSTRUCTION DEFINITION)!  

 IS DEFINED AS:

  Yr : DINT  (year)
  Mo : DINT  (month)
  Da : DINT  (day)
  Hr : DINT  (hour)
  Min : DINT  (minute)
  Sec : DINT  (second)
  uSec : DINT  (microsecond)]]>
</AdditionalHelpText>
<Parameters>
<Parameter Name="EnableIn" DataType="BOOL" Usage="Input" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="false">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Enable Input - System Defined Parameter]]>
</Description>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="EnableOut" DataType="BOOL" Usage="Output" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="false">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Enable Output - System Defined Parameter]]>
</Description>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Ref_DT1" DataType="DateTime" Usage="InOut" Required="true" Visible="true">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Date and Time input #1]]>
</Description>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Ref_DT2" DataType="DateTime" Usage="InOut" Required="true" Visible="true">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Date and Time input #2]]>
</Description>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Out" DataType="BOOL" Usage="Output" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="true">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Result: 1 if DT1 is Not Equal to DT2]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><DataValue DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
</Parameters>
<LocalTags>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_Out" DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Work Register: internal Output]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><DataValue DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_Null" DataType="DateTime">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Null Date and Time (amount of time = 0)]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><Structure DataType="DateTime">
<DataValueMember Name="Yr" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Mo" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Da" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Hr" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Min" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Sec" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="uSec" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</Structure>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_DT2" DataType="DateTime">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Result of Ref_DT2 + T_Now]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><Structure DataType="DateTime">
<DataValueMember Name="Yr" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Mo" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Da" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Hr" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Min" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Sec" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="uSec" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</Structure>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_DT1" DataType="DateTime">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Result of Ref_DT1 + T_Now]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><Structure DataType="DateTime">
<DataValueMember Name="Yr" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Mo" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Da" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Hr" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Min" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Sec" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="uSec" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</Structure>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_TADD_DT2" DataType="T_ADD">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Backing tag for T_ADD for DT2]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>01 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><Structure DataType="T_ADD">
<DataValueMember Name="EnableIn" DataType="BOOL" Value="1"/>
<DataValueMember Name="EnableOut" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
</Structure>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_TADD_DT1" DataType="T_ADD">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Backing tag for T_ADD for DT1]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>01 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><Structure DataType="T_ADD">
<DataValueMember Name="EnableIn" DataType="BOOL" Value="1"/>
<DataValueMember Name="EnableOut" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
</Structure>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
</LocalTags>
<Routines>
<Routine Name="EnableInFalse" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[If rung is false, clear output ]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
ENABLE-IN FALSE LOGIC
============================================================
When EnableIn is false (false rung in LD, input of 0 in FBD),
the main Logic Routine is not scanned, and the output  is
not cleared.  We need this Routine to Clear  in that case.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTU(Out);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="Logic" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Compare: DT1 <> DT2 ?]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
T_NEQ:  TIME -- NOT EQUAL TO
============================================================
Revision 1.0-Example:  2008-Jul-02, DER
Release for V17 CD as Date/Time Examples
============================================================
Returns TRUE (1) in EnableOut and Out if Ref_DT1 is GREATER THAN
OR EQUAL TO (after or the same as) Ref_DT2
============================================================
POWERUP / INVALID STATE HANDLING
============================================================
This logic determines a comparison result every scan when enabled
(and sets EnableOut and Out to 0 every scan if on a False Rung or if EnableIn is cleared).
No powerup or invalid state handling is necessary.
============================================================
NORMALIZE THE INPUT DATES/TIMES
============================================================
This rung adds each of the input Date/Time parameters to a .
 The T_ADD instruction  its output to:
0 <= microseconds < 1.000,000
0 <= seconds < 60
0 <= minutes < 60
0 <= hours < 24
1 <= days <= 31 (and day is valid for calendar month/year)
1 <= months <= 12
valid years are about +/- 5.8 million

Remember that if A <> B, then A+C <> B+C, so we are OK to add.  And
it works if what we're adding is a Date/Time OR an Amount of Time!!!]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[CLR(Wrk_Null.Yr) CLR(Wrk_Null.Mo) CLR(Wrk_Null.Da) ,CLR(Wrk_Null.Hr) CLR(Wrk_Null.Min) CLR(Wrk_Null.Sec) ,CLR(Wrk_Null.uSec) T_ADD(Wrk_TADD_DT1,Wrk_Null,Ref_DT1,Wrk_DT1) T_ADD(Wrk_TADD_DT2,Wrk_Null,Ref_DT2,Wrk_DT2) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
COMPARE Wrk_DT1 <> Wrk_DT2
============================================================
Now that the two input parameters have been :
IF the Wrk_DT1 YEAR is not equl to Wrk_DT2 YEAR, or
the Wrk_DT1 MONTH is not equl to Wrk_DT2 MONTH, or
the Wrk_DT1 DAY is not equl to Wrk_DT2 DAY, or
the Wrk_DT1 HOUR is not equl to Wrk_DT2 HOUR, or
the Wrk_DT1 MINUTE is not equl to Wrk_DT2 MINUTE, or
the Wrk_DT1 SECOND is not equl to Wrk_DT2 SECOND, or
the Wrk_DT1 MICROSECOND is not equl to Wrk_DT2 MICROSECOND (whew!),
THEN Wrk_DT1 is THE NOT SAME AS (not equal to) Wrk_DT2,
and so Ref_DT1 is not equal to Ref_DT2.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[NEQ(Wrk_DT1.Yr,Wrk_DT2.Yr) ,NEQ(Wrk_DT1.Mo,Wrk_DT2.Mo) ,NEQ(Wrk_DT1.Da,Wrk_DT2.Da) ,NEQ(Wrk_DT1.Hr,Wrk_DT2.Hr) ,NEQ(Wrk_DT1.Min,Wrk_DT2.Min) ,NEQ(Wrk_DT1.uSec,Wrk_DT2.uSec) ,NEQ(Wrk_DT1.Sec,Wrk_DT2.Sec) ]OTE(EnableOut)OTE(Wrk_Out);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Normally there would be an OTE of  on the rung above,
but because we unlatch (OTU) the Out bit in the EnableInFalse routine,
we need to have all  references be OTL or OTU in order to avoid
an annoying verification Warning (duplicate destructive bit reference).
This warning appears in the user program even if this AOI is locked down....]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Wrk_Out) OTL(Out) ,XIO(Wrk_Out) OTU(Out) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
</Routines>
</AddOnInstructionDefinition>
<AddOnInstructionDefinition Name="T_SUB" Revision="1.0" RevisionExtension="Example" Vendor="Rockwell Automation" ExecutePrescan="false" ExecutePostscan="false" ExecuteEnableInFalse="false" CreatedDate="2008-04-22T16:58:05.312Z" CreatedBy="NA\dereed" EditedDate="2008-07-02T16:37:13.600Z" EditedBy="NA\dereed"
 SoftwareRevision="v16.03">
<Description>
<![CDATA[DateTime := DateTime - Time]]>
</Description>
<RevisionNote>
<![CDATA[Release for V17 CD as Date/Time Examples]]>
</RevisionNote>
<AdditionalHelpText>
<![CDATA[T_Sub : Subtract Date/Time minus Time to get new Date/Time

This instruction subtracts a given amount of Time from a Date/Time to arrive at a new Date/Time.  The new Date/Time is , that is, given as a valid (if possible) Gregorian Date and Time:

*  0 <= Microseconds < 1,000,000
*  0 <= Seconds < 60    (NOTE: this instruction cannot add leap seconds;  sorry!)
*  0 <= Minutes < 60
*  0 <= Hours < 24
*  1 <= Day <= 31 AND Date is a Valid Gregorian Date (see below)
*  1 <= Month <= 12

NOTE:  This instruction does NOT switch to Julian dates for dates before 1582 (or 1753 or whenever your place of interest switched to the Gregorian Calendar -- see Wikipedia on  for details)!  This instruction assumes the Gregorian Calendar extends  (about 5.8 million years) either side of  CE!  It DOES handle the Gregorian 4 / 100 / 400 year rules, so Feb. 29, 2000 is a valid date, but Feb. 29, 2100 is not.  It DOES NOT handle Daylight Savings Time hour offsets when the amount of Time added carries the Date/Time across summer/winter time boundaries.
]]>
</AdditionalHelpText>
<Parameters>
<Parameter Name="EnableIn" DataType="BOOL" Usage="Input" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="false">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Enable Input - System Defined Parameter]]>
</Description>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="EnableOut" DataType="BOOL" Usage="Output" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="false">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Enable Output - System Defined Parameter]]>
</Description>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Ref_DT" DataType="DateTime" Usage="InOut" Required="true" Visible="true">
<Description>
<![CDATA[DT (Date/Time) from which to subtract Time]]>
</Description>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Ref_Time" DataType="DateTime" Usage="InOut" Required="true" Visible="true">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Time to be subtracted from DT (Date/Time)]]>
</Description>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Ref_Out" DataType="DateTime" Usage="InOut" Required="true" Visible="true">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Date/Time = DT-Time]]>
</Description>
</Parameter>
</Parameters>
<LocalTags>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_Time" DataType="DateTime">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Negative of Ref_Time, to add to DT]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><Structure DataType="DateTime">
<DataValueMember Name="Yr" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Mo" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Da" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Hr" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Min" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Sec" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="uSec" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</Structure>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_TADD" DataType="T_ADD">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Backing Tag for contained T_ADD instruction]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>01 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><Structure DataType="T_ADD">
<DataValueMember Name="EnableIn" DataType="BOOL" Value="1"/>
<DataValueMember Name="EnableOut" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
</Structure>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
</LocalTags>
<Routines>
<Routine Name="Logic" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Subtract Date/Time minus Amount of Time to give Date/Time]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
T_SUB:  TIME -- SUBTRACT
============================================================
Revision 1.0-Example:  2008-Jul-02, DER
Release for V17 CD as Date/Time Examples
============================================================
This instruction subtracts a given amount of Time from a Date/Time
 to arrive at a new Date/Time
The new Date/Time is , that is, given as a valid (if possible)
Gregorian Date and Time:

*  0 <= Microseconds < 1,000,000
*  0 <= Seconds < 60    (NOTE: this instruction cannot add leap seconds;  sorry!
*  0 <= Minutes < 60
*  0 <= Hours < 24
*  1 <= Day <= 31 AND Date is a Valid Gregorian Date (see below)
*  1 <= Month <= 12

NOTE:  This instruction does NOT switch to Julian dates for dates
before 1582 (or 1753 or whenever your place of interest
switched to the Gregorian Calendar -- see Wikipedia on
 for details)!
This instruction assumes the Gregorian Calendar extends 
(about 5.8 million years) either side of  CE!
It DOES handle the Gregorian 4 / 100 / 400 year rules, so Feb. 29, 2000
is a valid date, but Feb. 29, 2100 is not.
It DOES NOT handle Daylight Savings Time hour offsets when the amount of
Time subtracted carries the Date/Time across summer/winter time boundaries.

NOTE:  For algorithms used for Gregorian Date and Days Between Dates, see:
http://alcor.concordia.ca/~gpkatch/gdate-algorithm.html
============================================================
POWERUP / INVALID STATE HANDLING
============================================================
This logic determines a comparison result every scan when enabled
No powerup or invalid state handling is necessary.
============================================================
NEGATE THE INPUT TIME, THEN USE T_ADD
============================================================
We effect subtraction by simply negating the amount of time to subtract, then adding.
(This assumes that T_ADD properly handles negative amounts of time.)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[NEG(Ref_Time.Yr,Wrk_Time.Yr) NEG(Ref_Time.Mo,Wrk_Time.Mo) NEG(Ref_Time.Da,Wrk_Time.Da) ,NEG(Ref_Time.Hr,Wrk_Time.Hr) NEG(Ref_Time.Min,Wrk_Time.Min) NEG(Ref_Time.Sec,Wrk_Time.Sec) ,NEG(Ref_Time.uSec,Wrk_Time.uSec) T_ADD(Wrk_TADD,Ref_DT,Wrk_Time,Ref_Out) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
</Routines>
</AddOnInstructionDefinition>
<AddOnInstructionDefinition Name="T_Clock" Revision="1.0" RevisionExtension="Example" Vendor="Rockwell Automation" ExecutePrescan="false" ExecutePostscan="false" ExecuteEnableInFalse="false" CreatedDate="2008-06-30T17:08:06.874Z" CreatedBy="NA\dereed" EditedDate="2008-07-02T16:32:25.794Z" EditedBy="NA\dereed"
 SoftwareRevision="v16.03">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Date/Time Clock]]>
</Description>
<RevisionNote>
<![CDATA[Release for V17 CD as Date/Time Examples]]>
</RevisionNote>
<AdditionalHelpText>
<![CDATA[This object manages the controller , providing date and time services, including:

 *  Accepts downloaded date and time for HMI or other sync source and sets the clock
 *  Reads the clock and provides the local date and time to other logic

NOTE: current date/time is provided as individual DINTs and as a DateTime type for
use with Date/Time Math instructions (T_ADD, T_SUB, T_GRT, etc.)

 *  Calculates and provides the day of the week for the current date

NOTE: Use T_DoW to calcuate the day of the week for ANY given date.

 *  Optionally sets a flag once a day to request a clock sync update
 *  Based on configured shift start times, determines the current production shift (for up to three shifts)

The controller clock can be synchronized by writing a valid Year, Month, Day, Hour, Minute and
Second into the appropriate Settings.  When the clock has been set, the Settings are returned
to  and the time is reflected in the corresponding Values and Status.]]>
</AdditionalHelpText>
<Parameters>
