</LocalTag>
</LocalTags>
<Routines>
<Routine Name="Logic" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
T_Clock:  CONTROLLER CLOCK HANDLER
============================================================
Revision 1.0-Example:  2008-Jul-02, DER
Release for V17 CD as Date/Time Examples
============================================================
This object manages the controller , providing date and time services
including:
* Accepts downloaded date and time for HMI or other sync source and sets the clock
* Reads the clock and provides the local date and time to other logic
* Calculates and provides the day of the week for the current date
* Optionally sets a flag every day to request a clock sync update
* Based on configured times, determines the current production shift
(for up to three shifts)

The time is provided as separate Values:
Val_Yr : DINT, 
Val_Mo : DINT,
Val_Da : DINT,
Val_Hr : DINT,
Val_Min : DINT,
Val_Sec : DINT,
Val_uSec : DINT,
Val_DayOfWeek : DINT,
Val_Shift : DINT)
============================================================
POWERUP / INVALID STATE HANDLING
============================================================
If any date/time update data have been received while the controller
is in PROGRAM, it will be  in the Setting registers when the controller
is placed in RUN and should be ignored/discarded.

If Clock Update Requesting is enabled via Configuration,
the bit to request a clock update is turned on during first scan.

============================================================
HANDLE RECEIVED DATE/TIME SYNC
============================================================
If a valid date and time have been received, and this is not the first scan,
store the date/time to the controller clock.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NEQ(Set_Yr,-1)NEQ(Set_Mo,-1)NEQ(Set_Da,-1)NEQ(Set_Hr,-1)NEQ(Set_Min,-1)NEQ(Set_Sec,-1)[XIO(S:FS) [MOV(Set_Yr,Wrk_DT.Yr) ,MOV(Set_Mo,Wrk_DT.Mo) ,MOV(Set_Da,Wrk_DT.Da) ,MOV(Set_Hr,Wrk_DT.Hr) ,MOV(Set_Min,Wrk_DT.Min) ,MOV(Set_Sec,Wrk_DT.Sec) ,CLR(Wrk_DT.uSec) ,SSV(WALLCLOCKTIME,,LocalDateTime,Wrk_DT.Yr) ,OTU(Wrk_UpdateReqd) ] ,[MOV(-1,Set_Yr) ,MOV(-1,Set_Mo) ,MOV(-1,Set_Da) ,MOV(-1,Set_Hr) ,MOV(-1,Set_Min) ,MOV(-1,Set_Sec) ] ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
GET CLOCK TIME
============================================================
This rung gets the current clock date and time and makes then available as Values.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[GSV(WALLCLOCKTIME,,LocalDateTime,Wrk_DT.Yr) MOV(Wrk_DT.Yr,Val_Yr) MOV(Wrk_DT.Mo,Val_Mo) MOV(Wrk_DT.Da,Val_Da) ,MOV(Wrk_DT.Hr,Val_Hr) MOV(Wrk_DT.Min,Val_Min) MOV(Wrk_DT.Sec,Val_Sec) ,MOV(Wrk_DT.Yr,Ref_Out.Yr) MOV(Wrk_DT.Mo,Ref_Out.Mo) MOV(Wrk_DT.Da,Ref_Out.Da) ,MOV(Wrk_DT.Hr,Ref_Out.Hr) MOV(Wrk_DT.Min,Ref_Out.Min) MOV(Wrk_DT.Sec,Ref_Out.Sec) MOV(Wrk_DT.uSec,Ref_Out.uSec) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
CALCULATE THE DAY OF THE WEEK
============================================================
This version of the day of the week is based on:

http://alcor.concordia.ca/~gpkatch/gdate-algorithm.html

(NOTE:  ALL divisions are INTEGER -- truncated -- divisions!)
F = ( month + 9 ) MOD 12
G = year - ( F / 10 )
Gregorian DayNumber [ D ] = ( 365 * G ) + ( G / 4 ) - ( G / 100 ) + ( G / 400 ) + ( ( ( F * 306 ) + 5 ) / 10 ) + day - 1
DayOfWeek = ( DayNumber + 3 ) MOD 7
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
This rung calculates the  and  functions shown in the algorithm above.
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[CPT(Wrk_F,(Wrk_DT.Mo+9)MOD 12)CPT(Wrk_G,Wrk_DT.Yr-(Wrk_F/10));]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
This rung calculates the remainder of the algorithm.
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
The  is calculated, and the MOD 7
(remainder after division by 7) is stored as the Day of the Week.

NOTE:  The  offset aligns Val_DayOfWeek as:
0=Sun, 1=Mon, 2=Tue, 3=Wed, 4=Thu, 5=Fri, 6=Sat]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[CPT(Val_DayOfWeek,(365*Wrk_G+(Wrk_G/4)-(Wrk_G/100)+(Wrk_G/400)+((Wrk_F*306+5)/10)+Wrk_DT.Da+2)MOD 7);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
REQUEST UPDATE OF DATE/TIME
============================================================
This rung sets a request every morning at 2:01 a.m., and on first scan, for a
date/time update from the (Local) HMI or another source.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Cfg_RequestUpdates)[EQU(Wrk_DT.Hr,2) EQU(Wrk_DT.Min,1) ONS(Wrk_UpdateReqdOS) ,XIC(S:FS) ]OTL(Wrk_UpdateReqd);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
DETERMINE THE CURRENT SHIFT
============================================================
This rung puts the current time (hours:minutes) and the shift start times on a
 from 0 to 1439 minutes of the day.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[CPT(Wrk_TodayMins,Val_Hr*60+Val_Min) ,CPT(Wrk_Shift1StartMins,Cfg_Shift1StartHr*60+Cfg_Shift1StartMin) ,CPT(Wrk_Shift2StartMins,Cfg_Shift2StartHr*60+Cfg_Shift2StartMin) ,CPT(Wrk_Shift3StartMins,Cfg_Shift3StartHr*60+Cfg_Shift3StartMin) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the current time (minute of the day) is before all the shift start times, the rungs that
follow won't determine a shift (as none of the shift start times are before the
cureent time).  Add 1440 mintes (one day) to the time to make ALL the shift
start times be to the  of the current time on the timeline.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LES(Wrk_TodayMins,Wrk_Shift1StartMins)LES(Wrk_TodayMins,Wrk_Shift2StartMins)LES(Wrk_TodayMins,Wrk_Shift3StartMins)ADD(Wrk_TodayMins,1440,Wrk_TodayMins);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the Shift 1 Start Time is the nearest shift start time to the  of the current time
on the timeline, we're in Shift 1.  Ignore shifts that don't exist, and ignore
shift start times that are to the  of the current time.  See if Shift 1 is the
 point to the left of the current time.

NOTE: If you have that rare facility with FOUR shifts, you can 
easily modify this logic.  You'll have FOUR rungs with THREE big branch
structures in each, instead of the THREE rungs with TWO big branches as below.
And you'll need a fourth item in each of the two rungs above, in an obvious fashion.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Cfg_Shift1Exist)GEQ(Wrk_TodayMins,Wrk_Shift1StartMins)[XIO(Cfg_Shift2Exist) ,LES(Wrk_TodayMins,Wrk_Shift2StartMins) ,GEQ(Wrk_TodayMins,Wrk_Shift2StartMins) CMP((Wrk_TodayMins-Wrk_Shift1StartMins)<(Wrk_TodayMins-Wrk_Shift2StartMins)) ][XIO(Cfg_Shift3Exist) ,LES(Wrk_TodayMins,Wrk_Shift3StartMins) ,GEQ(Wrk_TodayMins,Wrk_Shift3StartMins) CMP((Wrk_TodayMins-Wrk_Shift1StartMins)<(Wrk_TodayMins-Wrk_Shift3StartMins)) ]OTE(Sts_Shift1)MOV(1,Val_Shift);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the Shift 2 Start Time is the nearest shift start time to the  of the current time
on the timeline, we're in Shift 2.  Ignore shifts that don't exist, and ignore
shift start times that are to the  of the current time.  See if Shift 2 is the
 point to the left of the current time.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Cfg_Shift2Exist)GEQ(Wrk_TodayMins,Wrk_Shift2StartMins)[XIO(Cfg_Shift1Exist) ,LES(Wrk_TodayMins,Wrk_Shift1StartMins) ,GEQ(Wrk_TodayMins,Wrk_Shift1StartMins) CMP((Wrk_TodayMins-Wrk_Shift2StartMins)<(Wrk_TodayMins-Wrk_Shift1StartMins)) ][XIO(Cfg_Shift3Exist) ,LES(Wrk_TodayMins,Wrk_Shift3StartMins) ,GEQ(Wrk_TodayMins,Wrk_Shift3StartMins) CMP((Wrk_TodayMins-Wrk_Shift2StartMins)<(Wrk_TodayMins-Wrk_Shift3StartMins)) ]OTE(Sts_Shift2)MOV(2,Val_Shift);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the Shift 3 Start Time is the nearest shift start time to the  of the current time
on the timeline, we're in Shift 3.  Ignore shifts that don't exist, and ignore
shift start times that are to the  of the current time.  See if Shift 3 is the
 point to the left of the current time.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Cfg_Shift3Exist)GEQ(Wrk_TodayMins,Wrk_Shift3StartMins)[XIO(Cfg_Shift1Exist) ,LES(Wrk_TodayMins,Wrk_Shift1StartMins) ,GEQ(Wrk_TodayMins,Wrk_Shift1StartMins) CMP((Wrk_TodayMins-Wrk_Shift3StartMins)<(Wrk_TodayMins-Wrk_Shift1StartMins)) ][XIO(Cfg_Shift2Exist) ,LES(Wrk_TodayMins,Wrk_Shift2StartMins) ,GEQ(Wrk_TodayMins,Wrk_Shift2StartMins) CMP((Wrk_TodayMins-Wrk_Shift3StartMins)<(Wrk_TodayMins-Wrk_Shift2StartMins)) ]OTE(Sts_Shift3)MOV(3,Val_Shift);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="10" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
GENERATE STATUS
============================================================
This rung copies the internal Update Required latch to a public Status bit.
(This Wrk_ bit keeps outside objects from changing the latch state.)

Other status bits are determined in logic above and have no internal Wrk bit.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Wrk_UpdateReqd)OTE(Sts_UpdateReqd);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
</Routines>
</AddOnInstructionDefinition>
<AddOnInstructionDefinition Name="T_DIFF" Revision="1.0" RevisionExtension="Example" Vendor="Rockwell Automation" ExecutePrescan="false" ExecutePostscan="false" ExecuteEnableInFalse="false" CreatedDate="2008-04-08T21:16:05.802Z" CreatedBy="NA\dereed" EditedDate="2008-07-02T16:47:33.023Z" EditedBy="NA\dereed"
 SoftwareRevision="v16.03">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Time := DateTime - DateTime]]>
</Description>
<RevisionNote>
<![CDATA[Release for V17 CD as Date/Time Examples]]>
</RevisionNote>
<AdditionalHelpText>
<![CDATA[T_DIFF : Date/Time minus Date/Time gives Time Difference

This instruction is given two Date/Time points and determines the amount of time between them.  The result is given in Days, Hours, Minutes, Seconds and Microseconds.  (Years and Months are returned as zero, as the number of months is generally not used.)  The Date/Time parameters must be valid Gregorian Dates and valid clock Times:

*  0 <= Microseconds < 1,000,000
*  0 <= Seconds < 60    (NOTE: this instruction cannot add leap seconds;  sorry!)
*  0 <= Minutes < 60
*  0 <= Hours < 24
*  1 <= Day <= 31 AND Date is a Valid Gregorian Date (see below)
*  1 <= Month <= 12

... for results to be meaningful.

NOTE:  This instruction does NOT switch to Julian dates for dates before 1582 (or 1753 or whenever your place of interest switched to the Gregorian Calendar -- see Wikipedia on  for details)!  This instruction assumes the Gregorian Calendar extends  (about 5.8 million years) either side of  CE!  It DOES handle the Gregorian 4 / 100 / 400 year rules, so Feb. 29, 2000 is a valid date, but Feb. 29, 2100 is not.  It DOES NOT handle Daylight Savings Time hour offsets when the Dates cross summer/winter time boundaries.
]]>
</AdditionalHelpText>
<Parameters>
<Parameter Name="EnableIn" DataType="BOOL" Usage="Input" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="false">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Enable Input - System Defined Parameter]]>
</Description>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="EnableOut" DataType="BOOL" Usage="Output" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="false">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Enable Output - System Defined Parameter]]>
</Description>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Ref_DT1" DataType="DateTime" Usage="InOut" Required="true" Visible="true">
<Description>
<![CDATA[DT (Date/Time) to subtract from]]>
</Description>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Ref_DT2" DataType="DateTime" Usage="InOut" Required="true" Visible="true">
<Description>
<![CDATA[DT (Date/Time) to subtract]]>
</Description>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Ref_Out" DataType="DateTime" Usage="InOut" Required="true" Visible="true">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Result: Amount of Time between Ref_DT1 and Ref_DT2]]>
</Description>
</Parameter>
</Parameters>
<LocalTags>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_DaFromHr" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Number of Days to add from Hours]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><DataValue DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_HrFromMin" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Number of Hours to add from Minutes]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><DataValue DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_MinFromSec" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Number of Minutes to add from Seconds]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><DataValue DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_SecFrom_uSec" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Number of Seconds to add from Microseconds]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><DataValue DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_GD1" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Gregorian Day Number (calculated for given Y/M/D)]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><DataValue DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_G1" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Used in calculating Gregorian Day Number (function of Year and F)]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><DataValue DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_F1" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Used in calculating Gregorian Day Number (function of month)]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><DataValue DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_F2" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Used in calculating Gregorian Day Number (function of month)]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><DataValue DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_G2" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Used in calculating Gregorian Day Number (function of Year and F)]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><DataValue DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_GD2" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Gregorian Day Number (calculated for given Y/M/D)]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><DataValue DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_Out" DataType="DateTime">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Working accumulator for Output (Out)]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><Structure DataType="DateTime">
<DataValueMember Name="Yr" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Mo" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Da" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Hr" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Min" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Sec" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="uSec" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</Structure>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
</LocalTags>
<Routines>
<Routine Name="Logic" Type="ST">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Calculate Days between Dates and Time Difference]]>
</Description>
<STContent>
<Line Number="0">
<![CDATA[// T_DIFF : Difference between two Dates  (Date/Time minus Date/Time to get Amount of Time]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="1">
<![CDATA[// ]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="2">
<![CDATA[// This instruction finds the difference between one Date/Time and another (both assumed valid) and reports it as]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="3">
<![CDATA[// an Amount of Time.  The amount of time is given as a number of Days, Hours, Minutes, Seconds and Microseconds:]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="4">
<![CDATA[//]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="5">
<![CDATA[//  NOTE:  This instruction does NOT switch to Julian dates for dates before 1582 (or 1753 or whenever your place of interest]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="6">
<![CDATA[//    switched to the Gregorian Calendar -- see Wikipedia on "Gregorian Calendar" for details)!  This instruction assumes the ]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="7">
<![CDATA[//    Gregorian Calendar extends "indefinitely" (about 5.8 million years) either side of "zero" CE!  It DOES handle the]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="8">
<![CDATA[//    Gregorian 4 / 100 / 400 year rules, so Feb. 29, 2000 is a valid date, but Feb. 29, 2100 is not.  It DOES NOT handle]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="9">
<![CDATA[//    Daylight Savings Time hour offsets when one Date/Time is winter time and the other  is summer time boundaries.  This]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="10">
<![CDATA[//    instruction does not deal with Leap Seconds, and Date/Time parameters MUST be valid Gregorian, normalized Date/Time values:]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="11">
<![CDATA[//]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="12">
<![CDATA[//   *  0 <= Microseconds < 1,000,000]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="13">
<![CDATA[//   *  0 <= Seconds < 60]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="14">
<![CDATA[//   *  0 <= Minutes < 60]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="15">
<![CDATA[//   *  0 <= Hours < 24]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="16">
<![CDATA[//   *  0 <= Days <= 31 and a valid Gregorian Date (Feb = 28 or 29 days, etc.)]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="17">
<![CDATA[//   *  1 <= Month <= 12]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="18">
<![CDATA[//   *  year in the range (about) +/- 5.8 million]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="19">
<![CDATA[//]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="20">
<![CDATA[//  NOTE:  For algorithms used for Gregorian Date and Days Between Dates, see http://alcor.concordia.ca/~gpkatch/gdate-algorithm.html]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="21">
<![CDATA[//]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="22">
<![CDATA[//  Revision 1.0-Example:  2008-Jul-02, DER]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="23">
<![CDATA[//	Release for V17 CD as Date/Time Examples]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="24">
<![CDATA[//]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="25">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="26">
<![CDATA[// Add Microseconds]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="27">
<![CDATA[Wrk_Out.uSec := (Ref_DT1.uSec-Ref_DT2.uSec+1000000) MOD 1000000;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="28">
<![CDATA[// Carry excess Seconds]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="29">
<![CDATA[Wrk_SecFrom_uSec := (Ref_DT1.uSec-Ref_DT2.uSec+1000000) / 1000000 - 1;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="30">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="31">
<![CDATA[// Add Seconds]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="32">
<![CDATA[Wrk_Out.Sec := (Ref_DT1.Sec-Ref_DT2.Sec+Wrk_SecFrom_uSec+60) MOD 60;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="33">
<![CDATA[// Carry excess Minutes]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="34">
<![CDATA[Wrk_MinFromSec := (Ref_DT1.Sec-Ref_DT2.Sec+Wrk_SecFrom_uSec+60) / 60 - 1;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="35">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="36">
<![CDATA[// Add Minutes]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="37">
<![CDATA[Wrk_Out.Min := (Ref_DT1.Min-Ref_DT2.Min+Wrk_MinFromSec+60) MOD 60;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="38">
<![CDATA[// Carry excess Hours]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="39">
<![CDATA[Wrk_HrFromMin := (Ref_DT1.Min-Ref_DT2.Min+Wrk_MinFromSec+60) / 60 - 1;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="40">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="41">
<![CDATA[// Add Hours]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="42">
<![CDATA[Wrk_Out.Hr := (Ref_DT1.Hr-Ref_DT2.Hr+Wrk_HrFromMin+24) MOD 24;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="43">
<![CDATA[// Carry excess Days]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="44">
<![CDATA[Wrk_DaFromHr := (Ref_DT1.Hr-Ref_DT2.Hr+Wrk_HrFromMin+24) / 24 - 1;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="45">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="46">
<![CDATA[// That takes care of the time.  To add the days, we need to compute a Gregorian Day Number from the input Date,]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="47">
<![CDATA[// then add the days and compute a Date from the new total Gregorian Day Number.  This takes care of the days in the months.]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="48">
<![CDATA[// (After thet, we'll add the Months and Years like we did with the time.)]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="49">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="50">
<![CDATA[// Compute the Gregorian Day Number for the input Date]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="51">
<![CDATA[Wrk_F1 := (Ref_DT1.Mo+9) MOD 12;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="52">
<![CDATA[Wrk_G1 := Ref_DT1.Yr - Wrk_F1/10;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="53">
<![CDATA[Wrk_GD1 := 365*Wrk_G1+Wrk_G1/4-Wrk_G1/100+Wrk_G1/400+(Wrk_F1*306+5)/10+Ref_DT1.Da-1;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="54">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="55">
<![CDATA[Wrk_F2 := (Ref_DT2.Mo+9) MOD 12;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="56">
<![CDATA[Wrk_G2 := Ref_DT2.Yr - Wrk_F2/10;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="57">
<![CDATA[Wrk_GD2 := 365*Wrk_G2+Wrk_G2/4-Wrk_G2/100+Wrk_G2/400+(Wrk_F2*306+5)/10+Ref_DT2.Da-1;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="58">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="59">
<![CDATA[Wrk_Out.Da := Wrk_GD1 - Wrk_GD2 + Wrk_DaFromHr;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="60">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="61">
<![CDATA[// If the number of Days is negative, we need to bump it up by one and subtract 23 hours 59 minutes]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="62">
<![CDATA[//  59 seconds 1,000,000 microseconds (same amount of time) to make result look right...]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="63">
<![CDATA[//  Otherwise instead of -1 uSec we get -1 day +23 hours +59 minutes +59 seconds +999,999 microseconds]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="64">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="65">
<![CDATA[If ( Wrk_Out.Da < 0 ) then]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="66">
<![CDATA[	Wrk_Out.Da := Wrk_Out.Da + 1;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="67">
<![CDATA[	Wrk_Out.Hr := Wrk_Out.Hr - 23;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="68">
<![CDATA[	Wrk_Out.Min := Wrk_Out.Min - 59;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="69">
<![CDATA[	Wrk_Out.Sec := Wrk_Out.Sec - 59;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="70">
<![CDATA[	Wrk_Out.uSec := Wrk_Out.uSec - 1000000;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="71">
<![CDATA[	If ( Wrk_Out.uSec = -1000000 ) then]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="72">
<![CDATA[		Wrk_Out.uSec := 0;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="73">
<![CDATA[		Wrk_Out.Sec := Wrk_Out.Sec - 1;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="74">
<![CDATA[	End_If;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="75">
<![CDATA[	If ( Wrk_Out.Sec = -60 ) then]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="76">
<![CDATA[		Wrk_Out.Sec := 0;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="77">
<![CDATA[		Wrk_Out.Min := Wrk_Out.Min - 1;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="78">
<![CDATA[	End_If;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="79">
<![CDATA[	If ( Wrk_Out.Min = -60 ) then]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="80">
<![CDATA[		Wrk_Out.Min := 0;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="81">
<![CDATA[		Wrk_Out.Hr := Wrk_Out.Hr - 1;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="82">
<![CDATA[	End_If;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="83">
<![CDATA[	If ( Wrk_Out.Hr = -24 ) then]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="84">
<![CDATA[		Wrk_Out.Hr := 0;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="85">
<![CDATA[		Wrk_Out.Da := Wrk_Out.Da - 1;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="86">
<![CDATA[	End_If;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="87">
<![CDATA[End_If;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="88">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="89">
<![CDATA[// Copy the final numbers to the Output tag]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="90">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="91">
<![CDATA[Ref_Out.Da := Wrk_Out.Da;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="92">
<![CDATA[Ref_Out.Hr := Wrk_Out.Hr;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="93">
<![CDATA[Ref_Out.Min := Wrk_Out.Min;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="94">
<![CDATA[Ref_Out.Sec := Wrk_Out.Sec;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="95">
<![CDATA[Ref_Out.uSec := Wrk_Out.uSec;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="96">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="97">
<![CDATA[// No Months]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="98">
<![CDATA[Ref_Out.Mo := 0;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="99">
<![CDATA[// No Years]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="100">
<![CDATA[Ref_Out.Yr := 0;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="101">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
</STContent>
</Routine>
</Routines>
</AddOnInstructionDefinition>
<AddOnInstructionDefinition Name="T_Valid" Revision="1.0" RevisionExtension="Example" Vendor="Rockwell Automation" ExecutePrescan="false" ExecutePostscan="false" ExecuteEnableInFalse="false" CreatedDate="2007-09-07T20:09:49.027Z" CreatedBy="NA\dereed" EditedDate="2008-07-02T16:42:07.342Z" EditedBy="NA\dereed"
 SoftwareRevision="v16.03">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Is DateTime Valid?]]>
</Description>
<RevisionNote>
<![CDATA[Release for V17 CD as Date/Time Examples]]>
</RevisionNote>
<AdditionalHelpText>
<![CDATA[This instruction tests the given DateTime variable and verifies that it is a valid calendar date and clock time, as follows:

  *  0 <= Microseconds < 1,000,000
  *  0 <= Seconds < 60    (NOTE: this instruction cannot check leap seconds;  sorry!
  *  0 <= Minutes < 60
  *  0 <= Hours < 24
  *  1 <= Day <= 31 AND Day is Valid for Gregorian Date (28, 29, 30 or 31 days in month, see below)
  *  1 <= Month <= 12
  *  Year is within the range of dates that this instruction can calculate a Gregorian day number (about +/- 5.8 million years)

  NOTE:  This instruction does NOT switch to Julian dates for dates before 1582 (or 1753 or whenever your place of interest switched to the Gregorian Calendar (see Wikipedia on Gregorian Calendar for details)!  This instruction assumes the Gregorian Calendar extends  (at least 5.8 million years) either side of !  It DOES handle the Gregorian 4 / 100 / 400 year rules, so Feb. 29, 2000 is a valid date, but Feb. 29, 2100 is not.]]>
</AdditionalHelpText>
<Parameters>
<Parameter Name="EnableIn" DataType="BOOL" Usage="Input" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="false">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Enable Input - System Defined Parameter]]>
</Description>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="EnableOut" DataType="BOOL" Usage="Output" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="false">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Enable Output - System Defined Parameter]]>
</Description>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Ref_DT" DataType="DateTime" Usage="InOut" Required="true" Visible="true">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Date and Time to check for validity]]>
</Description>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Out" DataType="BOOL" Usage="Output" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="true">
<Description>
<![CDATA[1 = Date/Time is valid (exists)]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><DataValue DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Sts_YrInvalid" DataType="BOOL" Usage="Output" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="false">
<Description>
<![CDATA[1 = Date is invalid because year is out of the range this instruction can check]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><DataValue DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Sts_MoInvalid" DataType="BOOL" Usage="Output" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="false">
<Description>
<![CDATA[1 = Month is Invalid (1 to 12)]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><DataValue DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Sts_DaInvalid" DataType="BOOL" Usage="Output" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="false">
<Description>
<![CDATA[1 = Day is Invalid (not within days for that month/year)]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><DataValue DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Sts_HrInvalid" DataType="BOOL" Usage="Output" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="false">
<Description>
<![CDATA[1 = Hour is Invalid (0 to 23)]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><DataValue DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Sts_MinInvalid" DataType="BOOL" Usage="Output" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="false">
<Description>
<![CDATA[1 = Minute is invalid (0 to 59)]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><DataValue DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Sts_SecInvalid" DataType="BOOL" Usage="Output" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="false">
<Description>
<![CDATA[1 = Second is invalid (0 to 59)]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><DataValue DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Sts_uSecInvalid" DataType="BOOL" Usage="Output" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="false">
<Description>
<![CDATA[1 = Microsecond is Invalid (0 to 999,999)]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><DataValue DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
</Parameters>
<LocalTags>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_F" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Used in calculating Gregorian Day Number (function of month)]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><DataValue DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_G" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Used in calculating Gregorian Day Number (function of Year and F)]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><DataValue DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_GD" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Gregorian Day Number (calculated for given Y/M/D)]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><DataValue DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_yyy" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Intermediate for year calculation]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><DataValue DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_ddd" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Intermediate for day calculation]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><DataValue DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_mmm" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Intermediate for month calculation]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><DataValue DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_y" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Calculated YEAR from Gregorian Day Number]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><DataValue DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_m" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Calculated MONTH from Gregorian Day Number]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><DataValue DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_d" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Calculated DAY from Gregorian Day Number]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><DataValue DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
</LocalTags>
<Routines>
<Routine Name="Logic" Type="ST">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Checks whether given DateTime is valid (exists on common calendar/clock)]]>
</Description>
<STContent>
<Line Number="0">
<![CDATA[// T_Valid : Check for VALID DATE / TIME]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="1">
<![CDATA[// ]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="2">
<![CDATA[// This instruction tests the given DateTime variable and verifies that it is a valid calendar date and clock time, as follows:]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="3">
<![CDATA[//]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="4">
<![CDATA[//  *  0 <= Microseconds < 1,000,000]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="5">
<![CDATA[//  *  0 <= Seconds < 60    (NOTE: this instruction cannot check leap seconds;  sorry!]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="6">
<![CDATA[//  *  0 <= Minutes < 60]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="7">
<![CDATA[//  *  0 <= Hours < 24]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="8">
<![CDATA[//  *  1 <= Day <= 31 AND Day is Valid for Gregorian Date (28, 29, 30 or 31 days in month, see below)]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="9">
<![CDATA[//  *  1 <= Month <= 12]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="10">
<![CDATA[//  *  Year is within the range of dates that this instruction can calculate a Gregorian day number (about +/- 5.8 million years)]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="11">
<![CDATA[//]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="12">
<![CDATA[//  NOTE:  This instruction does NOT switch to Julian dates for dates before 1582 (or 1753 or whenever your place of interest]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="13">
<![CDATA[//  switched to the Gregorian Calendar (see Wikipedia on Gregorian Calendar for details)!  This instruction assumes the Gregorian]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="14">
<![CDATA[//  Calendar extends "indefinitely" (at least 5.8 million years) either side of "zero"!  It DOES handle the Gregorian 4 / 100 /]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="15">
<![CDATA[//  400 year rules, so Feb. 29, 2000 is a valid date, but Feb. 29, 2100 is not.]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="16">
<![CDATA[//]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="17">
<![CDATA[//  NOTE:  For algorithms, see http://alcor.concordia.ca/~gpkatch/gdate-algorithm.html]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="18">
<![CDATA[//]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="19">
<![CDATA[//  Revision 1.0-Example:  2008-Jul-02, DER]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="20">
<![CDATA[//	Release for V17 CD as Date/Time Examples]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="21">
<![CDATA[//]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="22">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="23">
<![CDATA[// Check Microseconds]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="24">
<![CDATA[IF ((Ref_DT.uSec < 0) OR (Ref_DT.uSec > 999999)) THEN]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="25">
<![CDATA[	Sts_uSecInvalid := 1;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="26">
<![CDATA[ELSE]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="27">
<![CDATA[	Sts_uSecInvalid := 0;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="28">
<![CDATA[END_IF;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="29">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="30">
<![CDATA[// Check Seconds]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="31">
<![CDATA[IF ((Ref_DT.Sec < 0) OR (Ref_DT.Sec > 59)) THEN]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="32">
<![CDATA[	Sts_SecInvalid := 1;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="33">
<![CDATA[ELSE]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="34">
<![CDATA[	Sts_SecInvalid := 0;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="35">
<![CDATA[END_IF;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="36">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="37">
<![CDATA[// Check Minutes]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="38">
<![CDATA[IF ((Ref_DT.Min < 0) OR (Ref_DT.Min > 59)) THEN]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="39">
<![CDATA[	Sts_MinInvalid := 1;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="40">
<![CDATA[ELSE]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="41">
<![CDATA[	Sts_MinInvalid := 0;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="42">
<![CDATA[END_IF;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="43">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="44">
<![CDATA[// Check Hour]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="45">
<![CDATA[IF ((Ref_DT.Hr < 0) OR (Ref_DT.Hr > 23)) THEN]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="46">
<![CDATA[	Sts_HrInvalid := 1;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="47">
<![CDATA[ELSE]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="48">
<![CDATA[	Sts_HrInvalid := 0;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="49">
<![CDATA[END_IF;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="50">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="51">
<![CDATA[// Check Day (basic check, see below for more!)]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="52">
<![CDATA[IF ((Ref_DT.Da < 1) OR (Ref_DT.Da > 31)) THEN]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="53">
<![CDATA[	Sts_DaInvalid := 1;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="54">
<![CDATA[ELSE]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="55">
<![CDATA[	Sts_DaInvalid := 0;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="56">
<![CDATA[END_IF;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="57">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="58">
<![CDATA[// Check Month]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="59">
<![CDATA[IF ((Ref_DT.Mo < 1) OR (Ref_DT.Mo > 12)) THEN]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="60">
<![CDATA[	Sts_MoInvalid := 1;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="61">
<![CDATA[ELSE]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="62">
<![CDATA[	Sts_MoInvalid := 0;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="63">
<![CDATA[END_IF;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="64">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="65">
<![CDATA[// Check Year is in the range we can test]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="66">
<![CDATA[IF ((Ref_DT.Yr < -5879600) OR (Ref_DT.Yr > 5879600)) THEN]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="67">
<![CDATA[	Sts_YrInvalid := 1;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="68">
<![CDATA[ELSE]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="69">
<![CDATA[	Sts_YrInvalid := 0;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="70">
<![CDATA[END_IF;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="71">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="72">
<![CDATA[// If the Year, Month and Day are all valid in the base checks above, check that the Date is a valid Gregorian Date]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="73">
<![CDATA[IF (NOT(Sts_DaInvalid) AND NOT(Sts_MoInvalid) AND NOT(Sts_YrInvalid)) THEN]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="74">
<![CDATA[//  First, Calculate a "Gregorian Day Number" for the input Yr/Mo/Da:]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="75">
<![CDATA[	Wrk_F := (Ref_DT.Mo+9) MOD 12;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="76">
<![CDATA[	Wrk_G := Ref_DT.Yr - Wrk_F/10;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="77">
<![CDATA[	Wrk_GD := 365*Wrk_G+Wrk_G/4-Wrk_G/100+Wrk_G/400+(Wrk_F*306+5)/10+Ref_DT.Da-1;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="78">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="79">
<![CDATA[//  Now, given the Gregorian Day Number, calculate the calendar date]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="80">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="81">
<![CDATA[	Wrk_yyy := TRUNC (Wrk_GD +1.5)/365.2425;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="82">
<![CDATA[	Wrk_ddd := Wrk_GD - (365*Wrk_yyy+Wrk_yyy/4-Wrk_yyy/100+Wrk_yyy/400);]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="83">
<![CDATA[	IF (Wrk_ddd < 0) THEN]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="84">
<![CDATA[		Wrk_yyy := Wrk_yyy - 1;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="85">
<![CDATA[		Wrk_ddd := Wrk_GD - (365*Wrk_yyy+Wrk_yyy/4-Wrk_yyy/100+Wrk_yyy/400);]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="86">
<![CDATA[		IF (Wrk_ddd < 0) THEN]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="87">
<![CDATA[			Wrk_yyy := Wrk_yyy - 1;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="88">
<![CDATA[			Wrk_ddd := Wrk_GD - (365*Wrk_yyy+Wrk_yyy/4-Wrk_yyy/100+Wrk_yyy/400);]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="89">
<![CDATA[		END_IF;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="90">
<![CDATA[	END_IF;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="91">
<![CDATA[	Wrk_mmm := (100*Wrk_ddd + 52)/3060;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="92">
<![CDATA[	Wrk_y := Wrk_yyy + (Wrk_mmm + 2)/12;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="93">
<![CDATA[	Wrk_m := ((Wrk_mmm + 2) MOD 12) + 1; ]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="94">
<![CDATA[	Wrk_d := Wrk_ddd - ((Wrk_mmm * 306) + 5)/10 + 1;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="95">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="96">
<![CDATA[//  If the Input Year/Month/Day match the calculated Year/Month/Day, the date (day number) is valid.]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="97">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="98">
<![CDATA[	IF ((Wrk_m <> Ref_DT.Mo) OR (Wrk_y <> Ref_DT.Yr) OR (Wrk_d <> Ref_DT.Da)) THEN]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="99">
<![CDATA[		Sts_DaInvalid := 1;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="100">
<![CDATA[	END_IF;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="101">
<![CDATA[	]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="102">
<![CDATA[END_IF;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="103">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="104">
<![CDATA[//  If nothing is invalid, set Out to indicate a valid date/time; otherwise, clear Out]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="105">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="106">
<![CDATA[IF ((NOT(Sts_uSecInvalid)) AND (NOT(Sts_SecInvalid)) AND (NOT(Sts_MinInvalid)) AND (NOT(Sts_HrInvalid)) AND (NOT(Sts_DaInvalid)) AND (NOT(Sts_MoInvalid)) AND (NOT(Sts_YrInvalid))) THEN]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="107">
<![CDATA[	Out := 1;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="108">
<![CDATA[ELSE]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="109">
<![CDATA[	Out := 0;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="110">
<![CDATA[END_IF;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="111">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
</STContent>
</Routine>
</Routines>
</AddOnInstructionDefinition>
<AddOnInstructionDefinition Name="T_DoW" Revision="1.0" RevisionExtension="Example" Vendor="Rockwell Automation" ExecutePrescan="false" ExecutePostscan="false" ExecuteEnableInFalse="false" CreatedDate="2008-04-09T17:38:34.917Z" CreatedBy="NA\dereed" EditedDate="2008-07-02T18:03:23.892Z" EditedBy="NA\dereed"
 SoftwareRevision="v16.03">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Day of the Week]]>
</Description>
<RevisionNote>
<![CDATA[Release for V17 CD as Date/Time Examples]]>
</RevisionNote>
<AdditionalHelpText>
<![CDATA[T_DoW : Day of the Week

This instruction takes a given Date/Time, and, for the Date part, returns the Day of the Week
  (0=Sun, 1=Mon, 2=Tue, 3=Wed, 4=Thu, 5=Fri, 6=Sat)

If the given Date is INVALID, a flag is set (but the calculated Day of the Week is returned anyway...)

NOTE:  The Time part of Input Parameter DT (hours, minutes, seconds, microseconds) is ignored.

NOTE:  This instruction does NOT switch to Julian dates for dates before 1582 (or 1753 or whenever your place of interest switched to the Gregorian Calendar (see Wikipedia on Gregorian Calendar for details)!  This instruction assumes the Gregorian Calendar extends  (at least 5.8 million years) either side of !  It DOES handle the Gregorian 4 / 100 / 400 year rules, so Feb. 29, 2000 is a valid date, but Feb. 29, 2100 is not.]]>
</AdditionalHelpText>
<Parameters>
<Parameter Name="EnableIn" DataType="BOOL" Usage="Input" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="false">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Enable Input - System Defined Parameter]]>
</Description>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="EnableOut" DataType="BOOL" Usage="Output" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="false">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Enable Output - System Defined Parameter]]>
</Description>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Ref_DT" DataType="DateTime" Usage="InOut" Required="true" Visible="true">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Date/Time input]]>
</Description>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Out" DataType="DINT" Usage="Output" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="true">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Returned Day of the Week (0=Sun, 1=Mon,... 6=Sat)]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><DataValue DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Sts_InvDate" DataType="BOOL" Usage="Output" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="true">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Cannot compute Day of Week because Date is INVALID]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><DataValue DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
</Parameters>
<LocalTags>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_G" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Intermediate variable, function of Month, Year]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><DataValue DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_F" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Intermediate variable, function of Month]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><DataValue DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_TValid" DataType="T_Valid">
<Description>
<![CDATA[AOI Backing Tag for valid Date check]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>01 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><Structure DataType="T_Valid">
<DataValueMember Name="EnableIn" DataType="BOOL" Value="1"/>
<DataValueMember Name="EnableOut" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Out" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Sts_YrInvalid" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Sts_MoInvalid" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Sts_DaInvalid" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Sts_HrInvalid" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Sts_MinInvalid" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Sts_SecInvalid" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
<DataValueMember Name="Sts_uSecInvalid" DataType="BOOL" Value="0"/>
</Structure>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_D" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Work register for computed day number]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><DataValue DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
</LocalTags>
<Routines>
<Routine Name="Logic" Type="ST">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Determine Day of the Week for the given Date]]>
</Description>
<STContent>
<Line Number="0">
<![CDATA[// T_DoW : Day of the Week]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="1">
<![CDATA[// ]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="2">
<![CDATA[//  This instruction takes a given Date/Time, and, for the Date part, returns the Day of the Week]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="3">
<![CDATA[//    (0=Sun, 1=Mon, 2=Tue, 3=Wed, 4=Thu, 5=Fri, 6=Sat)]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="4">
<![CDATA[// ]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="5">
<![CDATA[//  If the given Date is INVALID, a flag is set (but the calculated Day of the Week is returned anyway...)]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="6">
<![CDATA[//]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="7">
<![CDATA[//  NOTE:  The Time parts of Input Parameter DT (hours, minutes, seconds, microseconds) are ignored.]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="8">
<![CDATA[//]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="9">
<![CDATA[//  NOTE:  This instruction does NOT switch to Julian dates for dates before 1582 (or 1753 or whenever your place of interest]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="10">
<![CDATA[//  switched to the Gregorian Calendar (see Wikipedia on Gregorian Calendar for details)!  This instruction assumes the Gregorian]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="11">
<![CDATA[//  Calendar extends "indefinitely" (at least 5.8 million years) either side of "zero"!  It DOES handle the Gregorian 4 / 100 /]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="12">
<![CDATA[//  400 year rules, so Feb. 29, 2000 is a valid date, but Feb. 29, 2100 is not.]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="13">
<![CDATA[//]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="14">
<![CDATA[//  NOTE:  For algorithms, see http://alcor.concordia.ca/~gpkatch/gdate-algorithm.html]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="15">
<![CDATA[//]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="16">
<![CDATA[//  Revision 1.0-Example:  2008-Jul-02, DER]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="17">
<![CDATA[//	Release for V17 CD as Date/Time Examples]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="18">
<![CDATA[//]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="19">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="20">
<![CDATA[//  First, check the received date to see if it is valid]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="21">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="22">
<![CDATA[T_Valid (Wrk_TValid, Ref_DT);]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="23">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="24">
<![CDATA[//  If the Year, Month or Day is not valid, set the Sts_DateInvalid flag; if all OK, clear the flag]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="25">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="26">
<![CDATA[IF (Wrk_TValid.Sts_YrInvalid OR Wrk_TValid.Sts_MoInvalid OR Wrk_TValid.Sts_DaInvalid) THEN]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="27">
<![CDATA[	Sts_InvDate := 1;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="28">
<![CDATA[ELSE]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="29">
<![CDATA[	Sts_InvDate := 0;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="30">
<![CDATA[END_IF;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="31">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="32">
<![CDATA[//  We've handled the validity check, now compute a "Day Number" whose remainder after division by 7 gives the day of the week.]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="33">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="34">
<![CDATA[Wrk_F := (Ref_DT.Mo + 9) MOD 12;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="35">
<![CDATA[Wrk_G := Ref_DT.Yr - Wrk_F/10;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="36">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="37">
<![CDATA[Wrk_D := 365*Wrk_G+Wrk_G/4-Wrk_G/100+Wrk_G/400+(Wrk_F*306+5)/10+Ref_DT.Da+2;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="38">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="39">
<![CDATA[//  If the day number is negative, the MOD won't work; add the biggest integer divisible by 7 to ensure it's positive!]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="40">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="41">
<![CDATA[IF (Wrk_D < 0) THEN]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="42">
<![CDATA[	Wrk_D := Wrk_D + 2147483646;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="43">
<![CDATA[END_IF;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="44">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="45">
<![CDATA[//  Finally, do the Modulo math to get the day of the week (0=Sun, 1=Mon, ..., 6=Sat)]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="46">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="47">
<![CDATA[Out := Wrk_D MOD 7;]]>
</Line>
</STContent>
</Routine>
</Routines>
</AddOnInstructionDefinition>
<AddOnInstructionDefinition Name="T_TtoS" Revision="1.0" RevisionExtension="Example" Vendor="Rockwell Automation" ExecutePrescan="false" ExecutePostscan="false" ExecuteEnableInFalse="false" CreatedDate="2008-04-30T19:38:42.235Z" CreatedBy="NA\dereed" EditedDate="2008-07-02T18:05:05.113Z" EditedBy="NA\dereed"
 SoftwareRevision="v16.03">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Date/Time to String]]>
</Description>
<RevisionNote>
<![CDATA[Release for V17 CD as Date/Time Examples]]>
</RevisionNote>
<AdditionalHelpText>
<![CDATA[This instruction takes the given date and formats it as a human-readable STRING.

For example, for the Date/Time:
   2008  12  31  23  59  59  999999
the return STRING will be (based on configuration):
   Wednesady, December 31, 2008  11:59:59.999999 p.m.

Options are provided for:
   * 24- or 12-hour time format (with a.m. or p.m. indicator on the 12-hour format)
   * displaying or not displaying microseconds
   * displaying or not displaying seconds
   * displaying or not displaying the Day of the Week
   * displaying day first (31 July) or month first (July 31)
   * displaying date in an ISO-format (YYYY-MM-DD)

This instruction checks for a valid (Gregorian) Date and Time and returns  and/or  as appropriate in the output STRING.  Valid dates/times are:
  *  0 <= Microseconds < 1,000,000
  *  0 <= Seconds < 60
  *  0 <= Minutes < 60
  *  0 <= Hours < 24
  *  0 <= Days <= 31 and a valid Gregorian Date (Feb = 28 or 29 days, etc.)
  *  1 <= Month <= 12
  *  year in the range +/- 5879600

The names of the days of the week and the months of the year, and the AM and PM indicator text can be changed by using the Local Tags Monitor for the instance.]]>
</AdditionalHelpText>
<Parameters>
<Parameter Name="EnableIn" DataType="BOOL" Usage="Input" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="false">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Enable Input - System Defined Parameter]]>
</Description>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="EnableOut" DataType="BOOL" Usage="Output" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="false">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Enable Output - System Defined Parameter]]>
</Description>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Ref_DT" DataType="DateTime" Usage="InOut" Required="true" Visible="true">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Date/Time as DINTs to convert to STRING]]>
</Description>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Ref_Out" DataType="STRING" Usage="InOut" Required="true" Visible="true">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Date/Time as STRING for display]]>
</Description>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Cfg_ISODate" DataType="BOOL" Usage="Input" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="false">
<Description>
<![CDATA[1=use ISO date format YYYY-MM-DD; 0=use pretty date]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><DataValue DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Cfg_DayFirst" DataType="BOOL" Usage="Input" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="false">
<Description>
<![CDATA[1=use ; 0=use ]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><DataValue DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Cfg_InclDoW" DataType="BOOL" Usage="Input" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="false">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Include name of the Day of the Week]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>01</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><DataValue DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Value="1"/>
</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Cfg_12Hr" DataType="BOOL" Usage="Input" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="false">
<Description>
<![CDATA[1=12-hour with am/pm, 0=24-hour with leading zero]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><DataValue DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Cfg_InclSec" DataType="BOOL" Usage="Input" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="false">
<Description>
<![CDATA[1=include seconds in output string]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>01</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><DataValue DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Value="1"/>
</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Cfg_InclMicrosec" DataType="BOOL" Usage="Input" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="false">
<Description>
<![CDATA[1=include microseconds in output string]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><DataValue DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Sts_InvDate" DataType="BOOL" Usage="Output" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="true">
<Description>
<![CDATA[0=OK, 1=Date supplied is not a valid Date]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><DataValue DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Sts_InvTime" DataType="BOOL" Usage="Output" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="true">
<Description>
<![CDATA[0=OK, 1=Time supplied is not a valid Time]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated"><DataValue DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
</Parameters>
<LocalTags>
<LocalTag Name="Cfg_MonthNames" DataType="STRING_20" Dimensions="12">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Names of the Months of the Year]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>07 00 00 00 4A 61 6E 75 61 72 79 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 08 00 00 00 46 65 62 72 
75 61 72 79 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
05 00 00 00 4D 61 72 63 68 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 05 00 00 00 41 70 72 69 
6C 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
03 00 00 00 4D 61 79 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 04 00 00 00 4A 75 6E 65 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
04 00 00 00 4A 75 6C 79 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 06 00 00 00 41 75 67 75 
73 74 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
09 00 00 00 53 65 70 74 65 6D 62 65 72 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 07 00 00 00 4F 63 74 6F 
62 65 72 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
08 00 00 00 4E 6F 76 65 6D 62 65 72 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 08 00 00 00 44 65 63 65 
6D 62 65 72 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="String" Length="7">
